Let the cost per meter to repave a street be $194.
Monica's street is 150 meters long. The cost to repave Monica's street is $194 \times 150$.
$194 \times 150 = 194 \times (100 + 50) = 19400 + 194 \times 50 = 19400 + 194 \times (100/2) = 19400 + 19400/2 = 19400 + 9700 = 29100$.
So, the cost to repave Monica's street is $29100.
Lewis' street is 490 meters long. The cost to repave Lewis' street is $194 \times 490$.
$194 \times 490 = 194 \times (500 - 10) = 194 \times 500 - 194 \times 10 = 97000 - 1940 = 95060$.
So, the cost to repave Lewis' street is $95060$.
The difference in cost is $95060 - 29100 = 65960$.

