Let Adam's current height be $h_0 = 40$ inches.
Let his growth rate be $g = 2$ inches per year.
Let the minimum height required to ride the roller coaster be $h_{min} = 4$ feet $= 4 \times 12 = 48$ inches.
Let $n$ be the number of years until Adam is tall enough to ride the roller coaster.
After $n$ years, Adam's height will be $h_n = h_0 + n \times g = 40 + 2n$ inches.
We want to find the smallest integer $n$ such that $h_n \geq h_{min}$, i.e., $40 + 2n \geq 48$.
$2n \geq 48 - 40$
$2n \geq 8$
$n \geq \frac{8}{2}$
$n \geq 4$
The smallest integer $n$ that satisfies this inequality is $n=4$.
Therefore, it will take 4 years for Adam to be tall enough to ride the roller coaster.

We can check our answer:
After 4 years, Adam's height will be $40 + 4 \times 2 = 40 + 8 = 48$ inches. Since 48 inches $= 4$ feet, Adam will be tall enough to ride the roller coaster after 4 years.

